* NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION — unreviewed design. Simulated results; models as stated; nothing has been built or measured.
* SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-S-2.0
*
* datasheet_models.lib — behavioural / level-1 models BUILT BY HAND FROM DATASHEET FIGURES for the
* open-aed charger and storage simulations (hardware/aed-main/sim/charger-storage).
* No maker SPICE model was obtained (2026-11-27): Littelfuse/IXYS publishes none for the D2 depletion parts
* that could be found; onsemi and Diodes Inc. model download links refused automated access or 404'd.
* Every figure below names its source. [DS] = maker datasheet; [WP-F]/[WP-E] = figures as read by the
* capture engineer in hardware/aed-main/capture-notes; [EST] = engineering estimate, not from a datasheet.
* These are NOT makers' models. They reproduce the datasheet's limit values, not the real curves.

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Depletion MOSFET, 1,000 V: Littelfuse/IXYS IXTT10N100D2
*   [DS] DS100326A(4/17) "Preliminary Technical Information", values as read in WP-F.md §3.1:
*   VGS(off) -2.5..-4.5 V (VDS 25 V, 1 mA); RDS(on) <= 1.5 ohm (VGS 0, 5 A); ID(on) >= 10 A;
*   Ciss 5,320 pF, Coss 300 pF, Crss 70 pF (VDS 25 V); IDSX(off) <= 10 uA at 1,000 V, -5 V, 25 C;
*   <= 250 uA at 125 C. BVDSX normalised 0.94 at -20 C (Fig. 11, curve reading).
*   Model: level-1 NMOS, VTO = voff (parameter), KP 4 A/V^2 [EST: gives IDSS ~ 24 A, gfs ~ 2 S at 0.5 A];
*   RD 1.4 ohm to make RDS(on) ~1.5 ohm; Cgs linear (Ciss - Crss); Cgd and Cds as junction capacitances
*   (M 0.5, VJ 0.7) fitted to Crss/Coss at 25 V; body diode; off-state leakage as an ohmic resistor
*   rleak (parameter; 100 Mohm = 10 uA at 1,000 V). Breakdown NOT modelled: the simulations report the
*   voltage a device is asked to block and compare it with the rating.
.subckt DEP_10N100D2 d g s params: voff=-3.5 rleak=100meg
M1 di g s s NDEP10
.model NDEP10 nmos(level=1 vto={voff} kp=4 lambda=0.001)
RDR d di 1.4
RLK d s {rleak}
CGS g s 5.25n
DGD g di DCGD10
.model DCGD10 d(is=1e-30 n=50 cjo=424p m=0.5 vj=0.7)
DBD s di DBODY10
.model DBODY10 d(is=1e-12 n=1.3 rs=0.02 cjo=1.39n m=0.5 vj=0.7 tt=500n)
.ends DEP_10N100D2

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Depletion MOSFET, 1,700 V: Littelfuse/IXYS IXTT2N170D2 (TO-268, same package as the 10N100D2)
*   [DS] IXYS DS100418B(02/12), read 2026-11-27 from a datasheets.com mirror of the IXYS PDF:
*   VDSX 1,700 V (TJ 25-150 C); BVDSX >= 1,700 V (VGS -5 V, 250 uA); VGS(off) -2.0..-4.0 V (VDS 25 V,
*   250 uA); IDSX(off) <= 25 uA at VDSX, 25 C; <= 500 uA at 125 C; RDS(on) <= 6.5 ohm (VGS 0, 1 A);
*   ID(on) >= 2 A; gfs 1.4/2.2 S; Ciss 3,650 pF, Coss 206 pF, Crss 80 pF; Qg 110 nC; RthJC 0.22 K/W;
*   SOA 204 W at 1,700 V, 120 mA, TC 75 C, 5 s. Temperature coefficient of BVDSX not read (Fig. 12 is
*   a curve); ASSUMED the same as the 10N100D2 (0.94 at -20 C) [EST].
.subckt DEP_2N170D2 d g s params: voff=-3.0 rleak=68meg
M1 di g s s NDEP17
.model NDEP17 nmos(level=1 vto={voff} kp=0.6 lambda=0.001)
RDR d di 6.0
RLK d s {rleak}
CGS g s 3.57n
DGD g di DCGD17
.model DCGD17 d(is=1e-30 n=50 cjo=485p m=0.5 vj=0.7)
DBD s di DBODY17
.model DBODY17 d(is=1e-12 n=1.3 rs=0.1 cjo=760p m=0.5 vj=0.7 tt=2.8u)
.ends DEP_2N170D2

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Generic depletion MOSFET with every figure a parameter, so one netlist can switch part:
*   dev = 1 -> IXTT10N100D2 values above; dev = 2 -> IXTT2N170D2 values above (see DEPSEL below).
.subckt DEPMOS d g s params: voff=-3.5 rleak=100meg kp=4 rd=1.4 cgs=5.25n cgd0=424p cds0=1.39n
M1 di g s s NDEPG
.model NDEPG nmos(level=1 vto={voff} kp={kp} lambda=0.001)
RDR d di {rd}
RLK d s {rleak}
CGS g s {cgs}
DGD g di DCGDG
.model DCGDG d(is=1e-30 n=50 cjo={cgd0} m=0.5 vj=0.7)
DBD s di DBODYG
.model DBODYG d(is=1e-12 n=1.3 rs=0.05 cjo={cds0} m=0.5 vj=0.7 tt=1u)
.ends DEPMOS
* Parameter sets (use in a netlist as .param expressions of 'dev'):
*   kp      dev1 4      dev2 0.6        rd   dev1 1.4   dev2 6.0
*   cgs     dev1 5.25n  dev2 3.57n      cgd0 dev1 424p  dev2 485p     cds0 dev1 1.39n dev2 760p
*   voff nominal dev1 -3.5 (+-1.0)  dev2 -3.0 (+-1.0)
*   rleak at max datasheet leakage: dev1 25 C 100M, 70 C 23.5M, -20 C 426M;
*                                   dev2 25 C 68M,  70 C 17.7M, -20 C 262M  (log interpolation [EST])
*   rating VDSX: dev1 1,000 V (940 V at -20 C, Fig. 11); dev2 1,700 V (1,598 V at -20 C ASSUMED same factor)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* GP02-40 4 kV small-signal rectifier (proposed gate-steering diode, not on the sheets).
* [DS] Vishay GP02-40 (datasheet 88523, as recalled; NOT re-read 2026-11-27 [UNVERIFIED]): VRRM 4,000 V,
* IF(AV) 0.25 A, VF <= 3.0 V at 0.25 A, IR <= 5 uA at VRRM 25 C. Leakage modelled as 2 Gohm at 25 C.
.subckt GP0240 a k
D1 a k DGP02
RLK a k 2g
.model DGP02 d(is=1e-10 n=3.2 rs=1 bv=4200 ibv=5u cjo=5p tt=2u)
.ends GP0240

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* SMF15CA bidirectional TVS (gate clamp). [DS as quoted in WP-F §3.4]: VBR 16.7-18.5 V, VC 24.4 V at
* 8.2 A, IR <= 1 uA at 15 V. Two back-to-back junctions; RS from (24.4-17.6)/8.2.
.subckt SMF15CA a1 a2
D1 a1 m DTVS15
D2 a2 m DTVS15
.model DTVS15 d(is=1e-12 n=1 bv=17.6 ibv=1m nbv=1.5 rs=0.8 cjo=200p)
.ends SMF15CA

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* BAT54 Schottky (one half of BAT54S). [DS] Diodes Inc. DS11005: VF <= 0.24 V at 0.1 mA, <= 0.32 V at
* 1 mA, <= 0.40 V at 10 mA (25 C); IR <= 2 uA at 25 V; CT 10 pF. IS/N fitted to the max-VF points.
* Leakage at 60-70 C [EST] 1 uA/V as WP-F. Temperature via XTI/EG (Schottky EG 0.69).
.model BAT54 d(is=2.0e-8 n=1.15 rs=1.5 bv=30 ibv=10u cjo=10p m=0.5 eg=0.69 xti=2)

* BAV199 low-leakage diode (one half). [DS] Diodes DS30232: VF <= 0.9 V at 1 mA..1.25 V at 150 mA;
* IR <= 5 nA at 75 V (25 C); trr 3 us. Fitted [EST].
.model BAV199 d(is=2e-12 n=1.9 rs=1 bv=85 ibv=5n cjo=2p tt=3u)

* MMSZ4688 4.7 V low-current zener. [DS] onsemi: VZ 4.47-4.94 V at IZT 50 uA; IR <= 10 uA at 3 V.
* Breakdown softness NBV fitted [EST] so VZ falls ~0.2 V from 50 uA to 10 uA. Temperature coefficient
* NOT read from a datasheet: corners +-0.94 mV/K (relative coefficient tbv +-2e-4 /K) [EST]. bvz is a parameter for corners.
* Correction 2026-11-28 (simulation audit): this model used TBV1, which ngspice 42 does not recognise ("unrecognized
* parameter (tbv1) - ignored"), so tbv had no effect. It now uses ngspice's TCV (volts per kelvin, applied as
* BV(T) = BV - TCV x (T - TNOM)), so TCV = -tbv x bvz reproduces the intended relative coefficient. With tbv = 0 (the
* default, and every netlist outside held_detector.cir / ../rev3/held_sensor_rev3.cir) nothing changes.
.subckt ZENER a k params: bvz=4.7 tbv=0
DZ a k DZM
.model DZM d(is=1e-14 n=1 bv={bvz} ibv=50u nbv=4.8 tcv={-tbv*bvz} rs=20)
.ends ZENER

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* TLP187 photo-Darlington optocoupler. [DS] Toshiba TLP187 Rev 6.0 as read in WP-F §5: CTR >= 1,000 %
* at IF 1 mA, VCE 1 V; saturated CTR >= 500 % at 10 mA; VCE(sat) <= 1.0 V; dark current <= 0.2 uA at
* 200 V (25 C), <= 20 uA at 85 C; VCEO 300 V. LED VF fitted [EST]: 1.10 V at 1 mA, 25 C (isled
* parameter for corners); output = ctr x I(LED) collapsing below a ~0.75 V Darlington saturation knee.
* idark parameter. ctr is the low-IF CTR (WP-F derates to 500 % new / 250 % end of life).
.subckt TLP187 an ka c e params: ctr=5 isled=4.7e-14 idark=0.2u
DL an kx DLED
.model DLED d(is={isled} n=1.8 rs=10 eg=1.42 xti=3 cjo=20p)
VS kx ka 0
BC c e I = {ctr}*max(i(VS),0)*(1-exp(-max(v(c,e)-0.55,0)/0.12)) + {idark}*(1-exp(-max(v(c,e),0)/0.1))
RCE c e 1g
.ends TLP187

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* BSS138 N-MOSFET (release switch, OVP driver). [DS] onsemi BSS138: VGS(th) 0.8-1.5 V; RDS(on) <= 3.5 ohm
* at 4.5 V... 6 ohm max at 4.5 V (WP-E quotes 6 ohm); Ciss 27 pF. Level-1 fit [EST].
.model BSS138 nmos(level=1 vto=1.2 kp=0.12 rd=1.0 rs=0.5 cgso=1.2e-6 cgdo=0.5e-6 lambda=0.01 w=20u l=1u)

* MMBFJ177 P-channel JFET (release pilot). [DS] onsemi MMBFJ177LT1 Rev 9: IDSS 1.5-20 mA,
* VGS(off) 0.8-2.5 V, rDS(on) <= 300 ohm. PJF with VTO = -vp (pinch-off at VGS = +vp). beta fitted so
* IDSS = beta*vp^2 ~ 5 mA at vp = 1.5 V [EST]; vp is a parameter.
.subckt J177 d g s params: vp=1.5
J1 d g s PJ177
.model PJ177 pjf(vto={-vp} beta={5m/(vp*vp)} lambda=0.01 rd=20 rs=20 cgs=6p cgd=6p is=1e-14)
.ends J177

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* UX-F5B 8 kV / 0.35 A fast HV rectifier (Sanken). [DS as quoted in WP-E]: VF 11 V typ / 14 V max at
* 0.35 A; trr 70 ns typ / 150 ns max. Modelled as one junction with large N (stacked die) [EST]:
* VF 11 V at 0.35 A; ttr parameter sets stored charge (TT ~ trr).
.subckt UXF5B a k params: ttr=100n vfadd=0
D1 a m DUX
.model DUX d(is=1e-9 n=18 rs=4 bv=8000 ibv=1u cjo=3p tt={ttr})
VX m k {vfadd}
.ends UXF5B

* ES3D 200 V 3 A ultrafast (clamp steering). [DS] Vishay ES3D: VF <= 0.9 V at 3 A, trr <= 20 ns.
.model ES3D d(is=1e-9 n=1.7 rs=0.03 bv=220 ibv=10u cjo=45p tt=20n)

* SMCJ45A unidirectional TVS. [DS as quoted in WP-E]: VBR 50.0-55.3 V, ~73-75 V at 21-23 A [UNVERIFIED in
* WP-E]. BV 52.6 V nominal; RS (74-52.6)/22 = 0.97 ohm.
.model SMCJ45A d(is=1e-12 n=1 bv=52.6 ibv=1m nbv=1.5 rs=0.97 cjo=1.5n)

* BSC070N10LS5 100 V logic-level MOSFET (primary switch), modelled as a switch with Coss.
* [DS] Infineon: RDS(on) 7 mohm max at 10 V (WP-E uses 8.5 mohm at 5 V gate, 1.55x hot); Coss ~ 600 pF
* at 50 V [EST from the class]; body diode. One device; the sheet has two in parallel.
.model SWPRI sw(vt=2.5 vh=0.1 ron=8.5m roff=1meg)
.model DBODYP d(is=1e-11 n=1.2 rs=5m cjo=2.4n m=0.5 vj=0.7 tt=40n)
